{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyhedralDomination","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyhedralDomination","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DominationSqueeze"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.toPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.toPoly","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L158-L166","doc":"Every ordinary `Domination` is a `PolyDomination` on a linear order — the\npolygon has a single face. So the polyhedral setting is a strict generalisation\nand nothing already proved is lost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.trivialFace_separates_nothing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.trivialFace_separates_nothing","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L149-L154","doc":"**A `Face` on its own asserts nothing.** The trivial face separates no pair,\nso `squeeze_of_face_separation` has content only for a face exhibited to\nseparate — the LP test must actually be *run*, not merely posited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.trivialFace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.trivialFace","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L141-L147","doc":"The constant-`⊤` functional. It is a legitimate `Face` and separates\nnothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.face_val_add_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.face_val_add_eq","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L132-L137","doc":"Separation also pins the grade of the sum on that face: the dominant\nterm's reading survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.squeeze_of_face_separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.squeeze_of_face_separation","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L119-L130","doc":"**The face-membership test — the translation.**\n\nAn archimedean inequality *\"the cost strictly exceeds the budget, so the budget\ncannot absorb it\"* is replaced by a question about the Newton polygon: **does\nsome supporting functional strictly separate the two valuation points?** If one\ndoes, the conclusion follows with no ordered field, no `ℝ`, and no surreals.\n\nThat question — *is this point strictly below that one along some admissible\ndirection* — is exactly an LP feasibility test on the polyhedron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.Separates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.Separates","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L113-L115","doc":"The face **separates** `a` from `b` when it reads `a` as strictly\ndominant. This is the LP-feasibility predicate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.toDomination_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.toDomination_val","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L110-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.toDomination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.toDomination","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L98-L108","doc":"**Every face specialises a polyhedral valuation to a `Domination`.**\n\nThis is the bridge: after choosing a face, the entire `DominationSqueeze`\ntoolkit — strict domination, non-cancellation, the tower lemmas — applies\nverbatim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.mono","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L92-L92","doc":"The functional is monotone (implied by `map_inf`, kept as a field so the\nspecialisation below needs no lattice lemmas). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.map_inf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.map_inf","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The polyhedral meet becomes the linear `min` — this is what makes the\nface a legitimate reading of the polygon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.map_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.map_top","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Depth is preserved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.φ","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The functional, already lifted to the `⊤`-adjoined value object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Face","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L77-L92","doc":"**A supporting functional — a choice of face.**\n\n`φ` sends polygon data to a linearly ordered scale, carrying the polyhedral meet\nto `min`. Choosing such a `φ` is choosing the direction in which the polygon is\nread, i.e. selecting a face. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.le_val_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.le_val_add","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Newton-polygon / ultrametric law in polyhedral form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.val_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.val_neg","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Negation preserves the polygon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.val_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.val_zero","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Zero is infinitely deep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.val","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Polyhedral grade — a Newton-polygon datum, not necessarily a number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PolyDomination","kind":"structure","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PolyhedralDomination.lean#L58-L73","doc":"**Polyhedral domination** — a valuation into a *lattice*-ordered value\nobject, with the ultrametric bound stated via the meet `⊓` rather than `min`.\n\n`Domination` is the special case where `Γ` is linearly ordered (then `⊓ = min`),\nso nothing is lost; what is gained is that the value of an element can be a\npolygon datum rather than a single grade. ","signatureChunk":0}]}